FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode wrote most of `lib/index.js` and still owns most of what survives. The file has been edited by many people, but only a small part of the current code is from anyone else, and nearly all of that is old.

**Surviving lines (surviving-lines, scoped to `lib/index.js` at HEAD 62628c0):** 214 non-blank lines (238 counting blank lines), 62 commits.

| Author | Non-blank lines | Share | Commits |
|---|---|---|---|
| Troy Goode <<email redacted>> | 132 | 61.7% | 28 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 20 | 9.3% | 4 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 14 | 6.5% | 5 |
| Troy Goode <troy@laptop.example> | 12 | 5.6% | 1 |
| LuisEGR | 6 | 2.8% | 1 |
| Raymond Feng | 6 | 2.8% | 1 |
| max.laverse | 5 | 2.3% | 1 |
| 15 others | 11 | 5.1% | — |

- **Bus factor is 1.** Troy Goode alone holds 61.7% of the lines. Four authors are needed to reach 80%.
- **Only one author is active.** Within 365 days of 2026-04-12, only Troy Goode has committed, and that holds 67.3% of the lines. The other 32.7% belong to people with no commit in that window.
- **Likely one person under two addresses (proposal, not applied).** The two Troy Goode addresses would combine to 144 lines (67.3%). I haven't written a `.mailmap` entry. Run `surviving-lines --identities` to see the candidate lines, and confirm it is one person before merging.
- **Reformat commit set aside.** 62628c0, "style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes", rewrote 1,016 lines across four files. surviving-lines excludes it by default. Without that correction, Troy Goode would hold 111 lines (51.9%) and the bus factor would still be 1.
- **Credit moved to the original author.** Eleven lines from e64e854 (Alejandro Caravaca Puchades's "Allow array of matching conditions as options.origin") are credited to Alejandro even though Troy committed them. Six lines from f038e77 are credited to LuisEGR, who was the author of the change, not the committer.

**History (from `git log --follow`, not counted):**

- **2013:** Troy Goode created the file in "first commit" (bcd03d9, 2013-01-30) and was its main author through 2013 and 2014. Early contributions came from Simon Mansfield, Damien Klinnert, Eric di Domenico, Mathias Buus, and Typicode.
- **2014–2015:** Express 4 support, the `vary` module change, and the wider origin and regex handling. Contributors included Igor Soarez, Alberto Leal, Shane Tomlinson, Raymond Feng ("Optimize applyHeaders by removing the closure"), Eran Tiktin, and a run of changes by Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (regex and origin options) in May 2015.
- **2015–2018:** Smaller fixes from DracoBlue, max.laverse, Hannah Wolfe, Tom Arad, Benjamin Eidelman (a Safari pre-flight workaround), and Tomek Kopczuk. Douglas Christopher Wilson made several lint and header fixes.
- **2019–2026:** Activity is light. Troy Goode did the ESLint switch (fcd2b56, 2015, which is still counted as Troy's), and later "lib: annotate handlers" (b2005d9, 2026-04-10). The reformat commit (62628c0, 2026-04-12) was the last change.

The per-author line counts and the bus factor come from surviving-lines. The commit list and dates come from `git log`. The surviving-lines run covers only this file, so the repo-wide numbers in the ownership brief don't apply here.

=== ANSWER B ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log --follow --format='%h %an <%ae> %ad %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js && echo --- && git log --format='%an' -- lib/index.js | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && git blame --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && wc -l lib/index.js && ls lib
 - Bash: git show --stat 62628c0 | head -20 && echo --- && git blame -w --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && git show --stat b2005d9 | head -12 && git show b2005d9 -- lib/index.js | head -60 && echo --- && git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 lib/index.js | sed -n '1,40p'
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** Troy Goode wrote and maintained most of `lib/index.js`, from the first commit in January 2013 through the 2026 annotation pass. About 25 other contributors made smaller changes. The raw blame makes Fiona Formatter look like the largest author, but that's only because of a 2026 reformat.

**Who shaped it**

- **Troy Goode** (2013–2026): wrote the original file ("first commit", 2013-01-30). He added the case-insensitive header lookup, the `origin: false` shortcut, Connect support without Express, Express 4 support, the `vary` module, and the `pause`/`resume` handling for async middleware. He also made the 2.8.0 release and, in April 2026, added `// checked` annotations to the handlers (`b2005d9`). Those annotations look comment-only.
- **Douglas Christopher Wilson** (2017): fixed the `Vary: Access-Control-Request-Headers` handling for dynamic `allowedHeaders`, fixed a missing `methods` error, and did lint cleanups.
- **Alejandro Caravaca Puchades** (2015): added regex and array support for `origin`, and switched to `RegExp#test`.
- **Simon Mansfield** (2013): added the early `Origin` check and moved the credentials header so it's sent on non-OPTIONS requests.
- **Raymond Feng** (2015): optimized `applyHeaders` by removing a closure.
- **Others with smaller changes:** Benjamin Eidelman (Safari pre-flight workaround), Tomek Kopczuk and Igor Soarez (`Vary: Origin`), Shane Tomlinson (method name normalization), Mathias Buus (non-Express request/response methods), Saad Tazi (frozen options), Typicode (added `PATCH` to defaults), Tom Arad (`maxAge: 0` fix), LuisEGR (removed unused parameters), Chima Alaebo (removed an unreachable branch), and a few more.

**What's still in today's code**

- **Fiona Formatter's 2026 reformat (`62628c0`)** changed the indentation and quote style on about 428 lines without changing logic. That's why raw `git blame` credits her with 214 of the 238 lines.
- **Ignoring that reformat and whitespace** (`git blame -w --ignore-rev 62628c0 --ignore-rev b2005d9`), Troy Goode owns about 157 lines. The rest are spread across Douglas Christopher Wilson (22), Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (12), Raymond Feng (9), max.laverse (6), LuisEGR (6), and others.
- The defaults object (`origin: "*"`, the methods list, `preflightContinue`, `optionsSuccessStatus`) and the `isOriginAllowed` logic are still mostly from 2013–2016 commits.

I only checked the commit history and blame here. I didn't read the surrounding code or the other files in the repo, so I can't say how the code is used beyond what's in `lib/index.js`.

=== ANSWER C ===
COMMANDS RUN:
 - Bash: git log --follow --format='%h %ad %an <%ae> %s' --date=short -- lib/index.js && echo --- && git blame --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep -E '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && wc -l lib/index.js && git ls-files lib | head -50
 - Bash: git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep -E '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && git blame --ignore-rev 62628c0 -w --line-porcelain lib/index.js | grep -E '^author ' | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn && echo --- && git show --stat 62628c0 | head -20 && echo --- && git log --format='%h %an %s' -3 -- package.json && git log --format='%an' -- lib/index.js | sort | uniq -c | sort -rn | head -5 && git show b2005d9 --stat | tail -3 && git log -1 --format=%B 62628c0 | head -5
FINAL ANSWER:
**Short answer:** `lib/index.js` is the core of the `cors` middleware. Troy Goode shaped it most, and most of the code that survives today is still his. A 2026 mechanical reformat makes raw `git blame` look like someone else owns the file, so I ignored that commit to get the real picture.

**Timeline**

- **2013 (Troy Goode, Simon Mansfield, Damien Klinnert, Eric di Domenico):** The first commit (`bcd03d9`) was by Troy Goode. Early work added Connect support, origin callbacks, the credentials header, and the rule that most CORS headers belong only on preflight responses.
- **2014:** Troy added Express 4+ support and the `vary` module (`#30`). Shane Tomlinson normalized method names to uppercase. Alberto Leal fixed the `options.origin` callback.
- **2015 (busiest year for external contributors):** Alejandro Caravaca Puchades added RegExp origins and array origins. DracoBlue added exposed headers to preflight. Raymond Feng optimized `applyHeaders`. Troy moved the project to ESLint.
- **2016–2017:** Troy released 2.8.0. Douglas Christopher Wilson fixed the `methods` delegate bug and the `Vary` headers for dynamic `allowedHeaders`. Benjamin Eidelman added a Safari pre-flight workaround. Lint cleanups came from Chima Alaebo and Douglas.
- **2018–2021:** Tom Arad fixed `maxAge: 0`. LuisEGR removed unused parameters.
- **April 2026:** Troy's "lib: annotate handlers" (`b2005d9`) is the most recent substantive change. Fiona Formatter's "reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes" (`62628c0`) rewrote almost every line of the file (about 428 lines across `lib/` and `test/`) without changing behavior.

**Whose code is still in it**

Blame with `--ignore-rev 62628c0` (238 lines total, approximate, counting surviving lines):

| Author | Surviving lines |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | ~109 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | ~22 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (incl. alex94puchades) | ~16 |
| Raymond Feng | ~8 |
| max.laverse | ~6 |
| LuisEGR | ~6 |
| Simon Mansfield, Igor Soarez, Benjamin Eidelman, others | 1–3 each |

Without ignoring the reformat, Fiona Formatter's commit accounts for 214 lines. That's a formatting artifact, not authorship. Troy's share rises if you also ignore whitespace (`-w`) (~159 lines), because his original style is reflected in many lines the reformat touched.

**Caveats**

- The reformat commit author is listed as `fiona@formatter.example`, which may be a shared or tooling identity, so I haven't attributed the change to a specific person.
- Line counts measure surviving lines, not total contribution. Troy wrote most of the structure; other contributors' logic (regex origins, `Vary` handling, the Safari workaround) still appears in the file.
